.\" -*- mode: troff; coding: utf-8 -*-
.TH AMU\-TRIGGER 8
.SH NAME
amu\-trigger \- run post-install system cache and database triggers
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
\fBamu\-trigger\fR refreshes system caches and databases after packages
that provide relevant files have been installed or upgraded. It is
invoked automatically by \fBamu\-bin\fR(8) for every installed or
upgraded package, and can be run manually after low-level system
changes.
.LP
Each trigger checks that its helper command exists and that at least one
of the given packages actually provides the relevant files; nothing runs
otherwise.
.LP
Supported triggers:
.TS
tab(|);
l l.
fontconfig cache|fc\-cache \-sf
GDK-Pixbuf loaders|gdk\-pixbuf\-query\-loaders \-\-update\-cache
GIO modules|gio\-querymodules /usr/lib/gio/modules
GSettings schemas|glib\-compile\-schemas /usr/share/glib\-2.0/schemas
GTK2 input methods|gtk\-query\-immodules\-2.0 \-\-update\-cache
GTK3 input methods|gtk\-query\-immodules\-3.0 \-\-update\-cache
icon themes|gtk\-update\-icon\-cache
udev hardware database|udevadm hwdb \-\-update
X font indices|mkfontdir / mkfontscale
desktop MIME cache|update\-desktop\-database
shared MIME database|update\-mime\-database /usr/share/mime
.TE

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fI<pkg...>\fR
Run triggers considering only the named installed packages. With no
arguments, all installed packages are considered.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBAMU_ROOT\fR
Alternative install root (default \fI/\fR).

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR amu (8),
.BR amu\-bin (8),
.BR amu\-src (8)

